  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 17-layer stack on Al substrate: Layer 1 is Cr (50-100 nm), Layers 2-17 are 8 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs. HfO2 layers (even indices 2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16) bounded 180-240 nm. SiO2 layers (odd indices 3,5,7,9,11,13,15,17) bounded 100-200 nm. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with reduced adaptive step size for HfO2 layers. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized, 400-2000 nm spectrum. Score: weighted absorptance in 400-700 nm plus weighted reflectance in 700-2000 nm. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 17-layer optical coating deposited on an aluminum substrate. The stack comprises a single chromium adhesion layer (50-100 nm) followed by eight alternating HfO2/SiO2 bilayers, with HfO2 thickness bounded to 180-240 nm and SiO2 to 100-200 nm. Maximize average absorptance and minimize reflectance in the 400-700 nm band, while maximizing reflectance and minimizing absorptance in the 700-2000 nm band. Perform coherent transfer-matrix simulations at normal incidence and unpolarized light across the full spectrum.",
